          "note": "Table 1, Fig. 6a–d: νs(OCO) of bidentate HCOO* resolved by p-polarized IRRAS (negative Fano profiles, TDM perpendicular to surface; dissociative HCOOH adsorption, room temperature, UHV). On Fe₃O₄(001) (Fig. 6a/c): bidentate-bridging, two components — 1369 cm⁻¹ (tet site) and 1377 cm⁻¹ (int site), Epn coupling; paired νas(OCO) at 1555/1548 cm⁻¹ (tet/int); δ(CH) at 1373/1385 cm⁻¹ also observed with inverted Fano shape. On Fe₃O₄(111) (Fig. 6b/d): quasi-bidentate at 1335 cm⁻¹ (paired νas at 1588 cm⁻¹) and chelating at 1380 cm⁻¹ (paired νas at 1548 cm⁻¹); no bidentate-bridging here (Fe-tet spacing 5.9 Å too large). Chelating forms first (from 0.05 L); quasi-bidentate develops above 0.2 L."
